# Blind-restore variant XFAIL ledger (GATE-06).
#
# One entry per line for each blind-restore variant that is expected to
# fail until a tracked bug lands.  run_variant.sh reads this file to
# decide whether a red score is an XFAIL (exit 0) or a real failure
# (exit 1).  The LCSAS_VARIANT_XFAIL env var still overrides this file
# for ad-hoc runs.
#
# Format (whitespace-separated):
#   <variant>  issue=#<N>  expires=<YYYY-MM-DD>
#
# Rules enforced by tests/recovery_hardening/test_blind_variant_xfail_ledger.py:
#   * every entry MUST carry an issue=#N reference and a future expires= date;
#   * an expired entry FAILS the hardening suite -- the team must either
#     promote the variant (delete the line) or consciously re-date it in a
#     reviewed diff;
#   * lines starting with '#' and blank lines are comments.
#
# A variant that scores 15/15 while still listed here triggers a strict
# XPASS (run_variant.sh exits 1), forcing the ledger cleanup immediately.
#
# Promoted out (2026-06-15): tier1-missing (issue #227) — scored 16/16 on
# two consecutive blind runs (tier-1 binary absent → restore.sh rides the
# fallback path and recovers all data).  Ledger is currently empty; add a
# line here only when a new variant has a tracked, expected-fail bug.
